cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ck3bench in research, please cite it as below."
title: "ck3bench: the research harness runner over ck3agent"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Stebbins
    given-names: Harrison
version: 2026.11.0-dev0
# date-released is stamped at the first release (tests/test_release_metadata.py
# requires it for a release version and forbids it for a -dev one)
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/skullbloc/ck3bench"
url: "https://github.com/skullbloc/ck3bench"
keywords:
  - large language models
  - game AI
  - Crusader Kings III
  - experiments
  - reproducibility
abstract: >-
  ck3bench runs experiments over ck3agent, an LLM agent that steers Crusader
  Kings III's native AI: an experiment is one TOML file, the registration's
  conditions block is generated from it, and runs produce sealed bundles and
  reproducible tables.
